the seven schools.text:
Source Secrets of Magic pg. 238

The following seven schools are considered proper specializations of Thassilonian rune magic. In this paradigm, the Thassilonians considered divination magic to be something every wizard should learn but that none need take the effort to master. 

Abjuration (Envy)
 Runelords of abjuration specialize in protective magic and in suppressing all other magic to glorify their own. Prohibited Schools evocation, necromancy; Rune Spells initial: {@spell blind ambition}, advanced: {@spell competitive edge} 

Conjuration (Sloth)
 Runelords of conjuration use their magic to create what they need as they need it, and call forth servants to do their bidding. Prohibited Schools evocation, illusion; Rune Spells initial: {@spell efficient apport}, advanced: {@spell swamp of sloth} 

Enchantment (Lust)
 Runelords of enchantment specialize in magic that compels and controls the minds of others, often to fulfill their own needs and desires. Prohibited Schools necromancy, transmutation; Rune Spells initial: {@spell charming touch}, advanced: {@spell captivating adoration} 

Evocation (Wrath)
 Runelords of evocation channel raw destructive energies and direct them toward all who would oppose their will. Prohibited Schools abjuration, conjuration; Rune Spells initial: {@spell weapon surge}, advanced: {@spell zeal for battle} 

Illusion (Pride)
 Runelords of illusion use magic to create the perfect appearance and fool others through trickery, deception, and misdirection. Prohibited Schools conjuration, transmutation; Rune Spells initial: {@spell veil of confidence}, advanced: {@spell delusional pride} 

Necromancy (Gluttony)
 Runelords of necromancy tap into their constant hunger for more power and enhancing their longevity, potentially even unto undeath. Prohibited Schools abjuration, enchantment; Rune Spells initial: {@spell overstuff}, advanced: {@spell take its course} 

Transmutation (Greed)
 Runelords of transmutation not only transform objects to create value, but also transform and enhance their own power. Prohibited Schools enchantment, illusion; Rune Spells initial: {@spell appearance of wealth}, advanced: {@spell precious metals}

